WEBVTT


00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.028
(children singing )


00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.504
¶ When our weeping's over ¶


00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:09.099
¶ He will bid us welcome ¶


00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.906
¶ We shall come rejoicing ¶


00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:14.539
¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:17.015
¶ Bringing
in the sheaves ¶


00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.610
¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.143
- ¶ We shall come rejoicing ¶
- ( pig snorting )


00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.713
¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.659
- ¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶
- ( pig squealing )


00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.219
¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.629
¶ We shall come rejoicing ¶


00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:37.034
- ( squealing stops )
- ¶ Bringing in the sheaves ¶


00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.631
Now you've got drought here.


00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.302
You've got drought


00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.709
right here in Gatlin, Nebraska.


00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.976
And there's not gonna be
no harvest this year--


00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:53.111
not in this Lord's year
of 1963, there ain't.


00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.621
- And say why.
- All: Sin.


00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.316
Say that louder.


00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.416
Sin!


00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.324
Oh, we drown in sin here,


00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:04.091
- and there's no rain for our corn.
- ( snorting softly )


00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.564
- And why is that?
- ( children murmur )


00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:09.864
Preacher: Because of
all of the adults in this world.


00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.634
God has spoken to me
in a dream.


00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.300
And in that dream


00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:18.936
He said that
all adults are sinners!


00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:22.311
He said there's
not a soul here in Gatlin


00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.316
over the age of 19


00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.252
who isn't wallowing in sin,
loving it, even as they drown


00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:30.756
- like pigs in a mire.
- ( groaning softly )


00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.985
It says in the Good Book,


00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:35.995
"Suffer the children
to come unto me."


00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.759
And if this town has any hope,


00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:42.325
it's in you young people.


00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.233
And so I want you to shout it out!


00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.000
All: Sin!


00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:53.109
But, brothers and sisters,


00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:56.638
we know the old ways of God,
isn't it so?


00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.243
We know there's
a God of the Old Testament,


00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.946
as well as the New--


00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:04.855
the God of sacrifice,


00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:08.588
the God who walked
on the face of the earth,


00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:11.722
He Who Walks
Behind The Rows.


00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.665
All:
He Who Walks Behind The Rows.


00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.693
He Who Walks
Behind The Rows.


00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:20.069
God does speak to me
in my dreams,


00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:24.566
and God has told me
that it is now our time--


00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.738
time to make sacrifice,


00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.610
time to kill!


00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:32.480
( squeals )


00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:35.420
( snorting softly )


00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:39.016
Now the Good Book does say
that a child shall lead them.


00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:43.154
So do what God tells me
in my dreams to tell to you,


00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:48.998
and never go without water
or be hungry again!


00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.333
All: Praise God.
Praise the Lord.


00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:54.204
Praise God. Praise the Lord.


00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.606
Praise God!


00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.638
( radio static )


00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:06.243
( man speaking on radio )


00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:09.385
Man:
Hail Mary, full of grace,


00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:12.914
- help me win this stock car race.
- ( rock music playing )


00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.223
All right. Boogie.


00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:20.694
¶ Riding on the road
to nowhere ¶


00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:25.136
- ¶ Trying to keep love alive... ¶
- Woman: Turn it down!


00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.832
Do you want to break
my eardrums?


00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:29.433
Yes, Vicky.
Whatever you say.


00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.500
Man on radio:...who was
cited for reckless driving.


00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:35.947
¶ Be happy
if you'll just stay with me ¶


00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.506
( vocalizes )


00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:41.179
¶ I know everything
will be all right ¶


00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:44.349
¶ We'll laugh and we'll sing
all through the night... ¶


00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.483
- Vicky: Too loud, Burt!
- What's that?


00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.324
- ( music stops )
- You play it like that


00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.353
- just to get under my skin.
- Oh, come on.


00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.524
Your paranoia is
showing again, Vicky.


00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:56.228
Sometimes, I wonder
how I ended up married to you.


00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.635
By saying two little words.


00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:02.402
Shut up.


00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.740
( Burt sighs )


00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.972
( sighs )


00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:09.004
Nebraska.


00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.855
I'm hungry. Where are we?


00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.533
Nebraska.


00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.061
Yes, I know that.


00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:36.075
But where in the hell are we?
Where's the lunch stop?


00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:39.169
You've got the road atlas.
You should look it up.


00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:41.146
You still remember
how to read, don't you?


00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:44.547
Such a comedian.
Is that why we got off the interstate,


00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:48.213
to look at 60 miles of corn and listen
to the wit and wisdom of Burt?


00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:52.122
Just get off it, Vicky!
Will you just get off it?!


00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.852
( rock music playing )


00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:00.798
¶ Oh, well, they call me ¶


00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:03.825
- ¶ Sergeant Evil... ¶
- ( music gets louder )


00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:09.172
¶ But I just played a part ¶


00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:14.271
¶ They think
my eyes are tearing ¶


00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:20.651
¶ But they don't know me
at all, yeah! ¶


00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:28.418
( sighs )


00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.188
- ( music stops )
- I'm sorry.


00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:32.857
It's all right. It's fine.


00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:36.699
It's just that I've driven so far
on the interstate-- 1 500 miles--


00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:39.364
- and since you won't drive, l--
- You know I get migraines


00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:42.067
- when I drive for a long time.
- I know you do. I know, okay?


00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:44.576
That's why I asked you to navigate
for me on these secondary roads,


00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.635
and you said you would.


00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:53.942
( sighs )


00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.113
- Well?
- Where did we get off the interstate?


00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:58.248
Back in Grand lsland.


00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:01.822
The next town is...


00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:05.194
Gatlin.
It's about 10 miles.


00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:08.223
( boy wheezing )


00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:12.734
( groans )


00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:16.303
A wide space in the road.
Do you suppose we can go there


00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:18.970
and get something to eat?
Or does the almighty schedule say


00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:21.070
we have to go on until 2:00
like we did yesterday?


00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:23.878
All right. You know what?
I have about had it with you.


00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.975
( choking )


00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:28.782
As far as I am concerned,
we can call it quits right now.


00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.948
We can just turn around and see
that lawyer you wanted to see


00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.787
- because I have had it--
- Watch out!


00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:35.259
- No!
- ( tires screeching )


00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.489
( Vicky screams, gasps )


00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:44.833
( panting )


00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:49.471
Burt!


00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.475
A dog-- tell me it was a dog.


00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:59.275
It was a boy.
It was a little boy.


00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:01.445
He ran out of the corn.


00:07:05.158 --> 00:07:07.149
He's dead.
He's dead, isn't he?


00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:09.184
Oh, yeah.


00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.667
Congratulations, tiger.


00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:37.555
It's manslaughter!


00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:44.690
That's what they call it!
You took your eyes off the road!


00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.459
Well, don't you
wanna come see


00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:49.195
so you can tell
all your NRA buddies


00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:52.170
what you bagged
in Nebraska, huh?!


00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:57.632
Don't you wanna come
and see?


00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:02.070
What are you gonna do?!


00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:06.684
What are you going to do?


00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:10.385
Answer me!


00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:13.415
Answer me, you--
( panting )


00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:18.029
Answer me when I talk to you!


00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:21.289
Look at me!


00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:24.593
Look at me!


00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:34.068
How'd you handle it
over in Nam, huh?


00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:37.549
How'd you handle it in the hooches?


00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.744
What do you use?
Grease guns, right?


00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:41.480
Grease guns and Zippos!


00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:43.921
Settle down.
You're hysterical.


00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:46.948
( chuckles )
Oh, tell me. You crapped out.


00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:50.861
Big Vietnam War hero, huh?


00:08:50.897 --> 00:08:54.333
Purple Heart
and all that, huh?


00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:57.859
Come on, John Wayne!
What are you gonna do?!


00:08:57.904 --> 00:09:00.202
It's no time to go Section 8!


00:09:00.239 --> 00:09:02.104
You ran that little boy down.


00:09:02.141 --> 00:09:04.837
He was just a little boy,
you ran him down


00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:07.539
and you can't--


00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:20.787
( sobs )


00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:22.953
You're going to jail.


00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.025
- You're going to jail.
- Yeah?


00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:28.056
- Yeah.
- You're rabid.


00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:30.227
Okay. It's taken me
all this time to figure it out.


00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:32.499
You've got a terminal case
of rabies.


00:09:32.538 --> 00:09:34.267
Shut up.


00:09:34.307 --> 00:09:36.036
( Vicky pants )


00:09:44.216 --> 00:09:46.616
- What are you doing?
- Turning him over.


00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:50.053
- No. You're not supposed to touch--
- I wanna see what I did.


00:09:51.791 --> 00:09:55.158
- I'm sorry about this, fella.
- I don't wanna look.


00:09:57.863 --> 00:10:00.161
( sighs )


00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:04.302
( panting )


00:10:07.406 --> 00:10:10.967
His carotid artery and jugular vein
have been severed.


00:10:13.079 --> 00:10:15.138
His throat's been cut.


00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:18.474
Somebody scragged this kid--


00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:21.680
bayonet, maybe a kitchen knife,
a cleaver-- I don't know.


00:10:21.721 --> 00:10:23.712
It sure wasn't
a two-dollar buck.


00:10:28.127 --> 00:10:30.857
You don't go to any more Kiwanis
meetings after your throat's been cut.


00:10:30.896 --> 00:10:32.591
I sure learned that
in the jungle.


00:10:33.633 --> 00:10:35.794
You get 20, maybe 30 seconds,
before you--


00:10:35.835 --> 00:10:38.998
- That little boy is dead.
- Yeah.


00:10:39.038 --> 00:10:40.198
- You ran him down.
- Yeah.


00:10:40.239 --> 00:10:42.104
- And you killed him!
- Sure, I ran him down,


00:10:42.141 --> 00:10:44.041
but I didn't kill him.


00:10:44.076 --> 00:10:46.601
Look. Go on, look at him.


00:10:46.646 --> 00:10:48.238
I haven't gone crazy.
His throat's been cut.


00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:50.908
Why would anybody cut
a little boy's throat? Huh, why?


00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:53.350
You like the idea that I killed him
too much to let it go?


00:10:53.386 --> 00:10:56.287
- No. Of course not.
- Just look!


00:10:58.257 --> 00:11:01.055
- Please look.
- ( whimpers )


00:11:07.099 --> 00:11:09.567
( gasps, pants )


00:11:09.602 --> 00:11:11.194
- Hey hey hey.
- Oh!


00:11:11.237 --> 00:11:15.037
- Don't faint. Look at me.
- Okay.


00:11:15.074 --> 00:11:17.599
Don't look around.
Don't look around.


00:11:17.643 --> 00:11:21.204
- There's so much blood.
- His throat's been cut,


00:11:21.247 --> 00:11:23.147
and that corn over there
is all bent and twisted.


00:11:23.182 --> 00:11:24.376
- Where?
- Don't look around.


00:11:24.417 --> 00:11:26.385
Ow!


00:11:26.419 --> 00:11:29.081
Don't act suspicious.


00:11:29.121 --> 00:11:30.520
( pants )
Okay.


00:11:30.556 --> 00:11:32.456
- Okay?
- Yeah.


00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:35.687
Now we're gonna cover
this boy up


00:11:35.728 --> 00:11:39.687
- and we're gonna put him in the trunk.
- ( whimpering )


00:11:39.732 --> 00:11:42.292
- I'm sorry about this, Vicky...
- Okay.


00:11:42.334 --> 00:11:45.132
-...but we've gotta do this.
- Okay.


00:11:45.171 --> 00:11:48.163
( sobbing )


00:11:50.076 --> 00:11:53.876
Sure. Yeah.


00:11:53.913 --> 00:11:56.143
That didn't cut his throat--


00:11:56.182 --> 00:11:58.150
not all ragged
and jagged like this.


00:11:58.184 --> 00:12:02.280
No army sergeant ever showed
the finer points of hand-to-hand combat


00:12:02.321 --> 00:12:04.482
to this poor boy's murderer.


00:12:04.523 --> 00:12:07.959
No, he was as good as dead
when I hit him.


00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:11.326
- ( crackles )
- ( grunts )


00:12:16.368 --> 00:12:18.529
Okay.


00:12:25.177 --> 00:12:26.906
Get in.


00:12:26.946 --> 00:12:30.143
No. Driver's side.


00:12:30.182 --> 00:12:32.673
- You want me to drive?
- No. I want you to start the car


00:12:32.718 --> 00:12:35.152
and wait for me.
I'm gonna go take a look.


00:12:35.187 --> 00:12:38.179
I can see blood on the corn
where the boy came out.


00:12:38.224 --> 00:12:40.886
I think I saw something else.
It's hard to tell from the road,


00:12:40.926 --> 00:12:43.360
but you can hide an army in there.


00:12:43.395 --> 00:12:45.386
The Vietcong sure did.


00:12:45.431 --> 00:12:49.162
In the paddies of course,
not the corn-- like jungles.


00:12:50.503 --> 00:12:52.403
Scragged, right?


00:12:52.438 --> 00:12:54.099
- Someone scragged him?
- Yeah.


00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:57.007
Sometimes, I think you'd sell your soul
to the devil for it never to have ended.


00:12:57.042 --> 00:12:58.976
That way you could go on
doing sweeps and smoking dope


00:12:59.011 --> 00:13:01.479
for the rest of your life 'cause
that was the high point of your life,


00:13:01.514 --> 00:13:03.175
wasn't it, Burt?
Good old Vietnam, right?


00:13:03.215 --> 00:13:06.810
This isn't one of your damn
consciousness-raising groups, Vicky.


00:13:06.852 --> 00:13:09.116
Now get in the car.
That's an order.


00:13:09.155 --> 00:13:10.918
Screw your orders.


00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:14.759
Vicky, would you just do it?!


00:13:16.962 --> 00:13:18.725
( sighs )


00:13:22.868 --> 00:13:24.358
What's up with the gun?


00:13:24.403 --> 00:13:27.065
His throat was cut, right?


00:13:27.106 --> 00:13:30.337
They're probably gone,
but I don't wanna take any chances.


00:13:30.376 --> 00:13:34.039
Now get in the car,
keep the engine running


00:13:34.079 --> 00:13:36.411
and you'd better bug out
should anyone come out of there,


00:13:36.448 --> 00:13:38.973
no matter how innocent he,
she or they may look, okay?


00:13:39.018 --> 00:13:41.077
Do you understand?


00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.350
I don't wanna sit in the car
all by myself.


00:13:43.389 --> 00:13:46.950
At this point,
I don't really care what you want.


00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:50.394
How did I end up married
to a son of a bitch like you


00:13:50.429 --> 00:13:52.954
in the first place, huh?
I wonder about that.


00:13:54.433 --> 00:13:56.264
I wonder about that a lot.


00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:00.437
So do l, babe.


00:14:01.941 --> 00:14:03.602
I'm scared.


00:14:08.113 --> 00:14:10.172
Is that all right, sir?


00:14:10.216 --> 00:14:12.309
Is it all right for me
to be scared, sir?


00:14:12.351 --> 00:14:14.251
That's fine by me.


00:14:23.062 --> 00:14:25.053
( car engine starts )


00:14:57.963 --> 00:15:01.296
( panting softly )


00:15:12.511 --> 00:15:14.775
( flies buzzing )


00:16:06.465 --> 00:16:09.457
( continues panting )


00:16:20.179 --> 00:16:22.704
( car honking )


00:16:25.551 --> 00:16:28.076
( honking stops )


00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:30.418
( leaves rustle )


00:16:35.728 --> 00:16:38.697
( rustles )


00:16:42.234 --> 00:16:45.260
( honking )


00:16:47.973 --> 00:16:50.874
( quivering )


00:16:50.909 --> 00:16:53.901
( leaves rustling )


00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:01.246
( wood creaking )


00:17:26.612 --> 00:17:29.911
- Oh, God.
- ( engine stops )


00:17:29.948 --> 00:17:32.644
( keys jingle )


00:17:38.557 --> 00:17:41.685
Hey! Mr. Comedian!


00:17:45.497 --> 00:17:47.260
Where are you?


00:17:49.535 --> 00:17:52.003
It's not funny!


00:17:54.139 --> 00:17:56.664
Burt!


00:17:56.708 --> 00:17:59.370
I told you to stay in the car.


00:17:59.411 --> 00:18:01.504
I thought somebody was watching me.
I looked behind me


00:18:01.547 --> 00:18:03.538
- and I couldn't see you.
- Get in.


00:18:04.583 --> 00:18:06.642
I should've tied a string
around the antenna.


00:18:07.786 --> 00:18:09.686
I got lost in there for awhile.


00:18:09.721 --> 00:18:12.212
It's a good thing you called
when you did. Push over.


00:18:15.294 --> 00:18:18.127
Here, grab this.


00:18:18.163 --> 00:18:20.256
What is it?


00:18:20.299 --> 00:18:22.426
Is that-- is that blood?
Is that his blood?


00:18:22.468 --> 00:18:25.335
- Yeah, I guess so. Grab it.
- No!


00:19:02.508 --> 00:19:05.909
( thunder crashing )


00:19:19.758 --> 00:19:21.316
I was scared.


00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:23.328
Uh-huh.


00:19:23.362 --> 00:19:25.023
Afraid-- I was afraid.


00:19:25.063 --> 00:19:28.521
You went into the corn and it felt
like somebody was watching me.


00:19:28.567 --> 00:19:31.536
Well, maybe someone was.


00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:33.936
You know what I'm talking about.


00:19:33.972 --> 00:19:37.601
Someone was there, all right?
I could feel it too.


00:19:37.643 --> 00:19:40.908
I remember that feeling
from Do Luc.


00:19:40.946 --> 00:19:43.574
You don't forget that.


00:19:47.619 --> 00:19:50.213
- ( thunder crashing )
- What did you say the next town is?


00:19:50.255 --> 00:19:52.189
Gatlin.


00:19:52.224 --> 00:19:53.953
Does it look big enough
to have a police station?


00:19:53.992 --> 00:19:57.257
No, it's just a dot.


00:19:58.463 --> 00:20:01.057
That little boy was on foot, right?


00:20:01.099 --> 00:20:02.999
Gatlin is the only town for 80 miles.


00:20:03.035 --> 00:20:06.436
- He must have come from there.
- If you say so.


00:20:10.008 --> 00:20:12.533
( thunder crashing )


00:20:14.613 --> 00:20:17.047
Why? Why would anybody
wanna do that to a little kid?


00:20:17.082 --> 00:20:19.141
I don't know.


00:20:20.385 --> 00:20:22.819
( sighs )
We might get a better idea


00:20:22.854 --> 00:20:25.584
- if we look inside that.
- Hmm?


00:20:25.624 --> 00:20:27.649
Do you really think so?


00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.594
Probably not.


00:20:30.629 --> 00:20:32.324
It's worth a shot.


00:20:32.364 --> 00:20:34.355
Do you wanna open it?


00:20:37.469 --> 00:20:39.369
Okay.


00:20:44.843 --> 00:20:46.470
Hey...


00:20:48.213 --> 00:20:49.976
thanks.


00:21:10.535 --> 00:21:12.435
( radio static )


00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:18.273
Didn't we cross a barn
or something back there?


00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:20.210
No. It was deserted--


00:21:20.245 --> 00:21:23.214
no power feeds
from the road...


00:21:23.248 --> 00:21:24.977
no good.


00:21:25.017 --> 00:21:28.145
- I think you see everything.
- Huh.


00:21:28.186 --> 00:21:31.917
It freaks me out sometimes.
It really does.


00:21:31.957 --> 00:21:34.585
I just feel as if
this is my responsibility, Vicky.


00:21:34.626 --> 00:21:38.323
I hit him, even if he was
bleeding to death when I did.


00:21:38.363 --> 00:21:40.797
- You see, I don't see everything.
- ( static continues )


00:21:40.832 --> 00:21:44.632
I sure didn't see him.
I took my eyes off the road.


00:21:48.106 --> 00:21:51.234
We haven't seen a car
or a truck in like an hour.


00:21:51.276 --> 00:21:52.538
It's weird.


00:21:52.577 --> 00:21:54.841
Maybe Nebraska's playing
a home game.


00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:56.177
( static )


00:21:56.214 --> 00:21:58.546
Why don't you tell that
to your American Studies class


00:21:58.583 --> 00:22:00.517
when we get back home?


00:22:00.552 --> 00:22:03.316
"ln Nebraska,
radio hasn't been invented yet."


00:22:03.355 --> 00:22:06.722
- There's nothing at all?
- Zilch.


00:22:06.758 --> 00:22:08.658
The other knot is coming now.


00:22:08.694 --> 00:22:10.685
( boy shouts on radio )
Atonement!


00:22:10.729 --> 00:22:14.756
Only by the blood
of the lamb are we saved!


00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:17.360
"Atonement" is the word,
brothers and sisters.


00:22:17.402 --> 00:22:19.267
There are some that think...


00:22:19.304 --> 00:22:21.238
No wonder
we're coming in five-by.


00:22:21.273 --> 00:22:23.366
We're right on top
of the radio tower.


00:22:23.408 --> 00:22:25.171
Boy preacher: "...wilt thou be
besmirched by the world."


00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:28.611
Now is that what
the word of God teaches us?


00:22:28.647 --> 00:22:32.014
Holy Jesus!
When are they gonna know


00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:33.517
- that way is dead?
- Hmm.


00:22:33.552 --> 00:22:36.112
When are they gonna know
that the wages of the world


00:22:36.154 --> 00:22:39.715
are paid on the other side, that there's
no room for the fornicator?!


00:22:39.758 --> 00:22:42.852
- Children: No!
- No room for the defiler of the corn!


00:22:42.894 --> 00:22:45.454
- No vacancy!
- Vicky: Wha--


00:22:45.497 --> 00:22:48.466
No room for the homosexual!
No vacancy.


00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:50.593
- This drivel makes me sick.
- ( radio turns off )


00:22:50.635 --> 00:22:53.365
What did he say about the corn?


00:22:53.405 --> 00:22:57.171
- I wasn't paying attention.
- He said something about the corn.


00:22:57.209 --> 00:23:00.770
I know he did--
something weird.


00:23:09.755 --> 00:23:11.416
Hey hey!


00:23:11.456 --> 00:23:13.151
There is life in Nebraska.


00:23:25.303 --> 00:23:27.464
Are you sure anyone is here?


00:23:27.506 --> 00:23:30.407
It doesn't matter.
I just wanna use the pay phone.


00:23:30.442 --> 00:23:33.843
I have to report this... murder.


00:23:35.647 --> 00:23:37.615
Are you all right?


00:23:37.649 --> 00:23:39.674
Yeah. Yeah, I will be...


00:23:39.718 --> 00:23:43.245
as soon as we're 1,000 miles
away from here.


00:23:43.288 --> 00:23:46.223
Sunny and sinful California.


00:23:46.258 --> 00:23:50.126
The Rocky Mountains
between us and Nebraska.


00:23:51.930 --> 00:23:54.490
You got any change?


00:23:54.533 --> 00:23:56.296
Nope.


00:23:56.334 --> 00:23:59.098
I'll just dial the emergency operator.


00:24:46.685 --> 00:24:49.245
We'll be in town
in a few minutes.


00:24:59.731 --> 00:25:02.495
Looks like folks
in Gatlin got religion.


00:25:02.534 --> 00:25:05.731
I thought all folks
in Nebraska had religion.


00:25:05.770 --> 00:25:08.136
It sure sounds
that way from the radio.


00:25:08.173 --> 00:25:11.973
Mm-hmm. Have you been
reading the signs?


00:25:12.010 --> 00:25:14.001
"A cloud by day,


00:25:14.045 --> 00:25:17.537
a pillar of fire by night."


00:25:17.582 --> 00:25:21.279
When they called it the Bible Belt,
they sure weren't kidding.


00:25:21.319 --> 00:25:24.379
"Take this...


00:25:24.422 --> 00:25:26.583
and eat...


00:25:26.625 --> 00:25:30.117
saith the Lord,


00:25:30.161 --> 00:25:34.655
God of hosts."


00:25:36.601 --> 00:25:39.365
It's what they say
when they give you communion.


00:25:39.404 --> 00:25:43.807
Yeah? I bet they use cornbread
for holy wafer around these parts.


00:25:46.444 --> 00:25:48.810
- Got it.
- Attagirl.


00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:54.384
A shirt...


00:25:54.419 --> 00:25:56.444
a belt...


00:25:58.490 --> 00:26:00.583
What is this?


00:26:00.625 --> 00:26:03.093
That's a real golden oldie.


00:26:03.128 --> 00:26:05.426
Huh.


00:26:07.799 --> 00:26:11.098
Anything strikes you as funny
about that radio sermon?


00:26:12.537 --> 00:26:15.768
You were obviously never
the son of a preacher--


00:26:15.807 --> 00:26:19.368
dragged from tent to tent,
going to meetings,


00:26:19.411 --> 00:26:22.175
hearing every kind of evangelist
preying on the uneducated,


00:26:22.213 --> 00:26:25.774
the lonely and the weak
instead of praying for them.


00:26:25.817 --> 00:26:28.308
I had enough of that religious crap
to last me forever.


00:26:29.321 --> 00:26:31.118
I told you about it.


00:26:31.156 --> 00:26:34.216
Yeah, but didn't this preacher
sound young?


00:26:34.259 --> 00:26:37.228
A teenager, maybe, but that's what's
so monstrous about their whole trip.


00:26:37.262 --> 00:26:39.822
They like to get them
while their minds are still rubber,


00:26:39.864 --> 00:26:43.322
and all the emotional checks
and balances to put in.


00:26:43.368 --> 00:26:46.132
You should've seen
some of the ones I got saved by.


00:26:46.171 --> 00:26:48.503
Let's see, there was...


00:26:48.540 --> 00:26:50.838
Baby Hortense,


00:26:50.875 --> 00:26:53.002
the singing marvel.
She was eight.


00:26:53.044 --> 00:26:55.376
She'd come on singing
"Leaning on the Everlasting Arms"


00:26:55.413 --> 00:26:57.813
while her daddy passed the plate,
telling everybody to


00:26:57.849 --> 00:27:00.579
( deep voice )
"Dig deep now, brothers and sisters.


00:27:00.619 --> 00:27:03.110
Let's not let
this blessed child down.


00:27:03.154 --> 00:27:06.419
She does the work of our Lord,
the son of God."


00:27:06.458 --> 00:27:08.153
Jesus.


00:27:09.394 --> 00:27:12.522
- Oh my God!
- ( tires screech )


00:27:13.798 --> 00:27:17.256
It's just--
( whimpering )


00:27:21.172 --> 00:27:24.266
Wow. It's a fantastic piece
of workmanship.


00:27:24.309 --> 00:27:27.301
Real American primitive.


00:27:27.345 --> 00:27:29.438
It's hideous.


00:27:29.481 --> 00:27:32.917
- It's a blasphemy. Throw it out.
- No, the police will want to see this.


00:27:32.951 --> 00:27:35.545
- Why?
- I don't know. Evidence, maybe.


00:27:35.587 --> 00:27:38.283
Just throw it out!
Will you do that for me?


00:27:38.323 --> 00:27:40.587
Just throw it out.
I don't want it in the car.


00:27:41.593 --> 00:27:44.391
All right. I'll tell you what--
we'll put it all in the back for now.


00:27:44.429 --> 00:27:46.727
As soon as we see the cops,
we give 'em everything--


00:27:46.765 --> 00:27:50.064
the body, the whole works.
And we'll be done with it, all right?


00:27:50.101 --> 00:27:52.467
Do what you want, okay?


00:27:58.476 --> 00:27:59.909
You will, anyway.


00:28:08.553 --> 00:28:11.852
Boy preacher:
Behold...


00:28:11.890 --> 00:28:15.917
a dream that come to me
in the night.


00:28:15.960 --> 00:28:18.622
And in my dream
the Lord was a shadow


00:28:18.663 --> 00:28:21.393
that walked behind the rows.


00:28:21.433 --> 00:28:25.096
And God spoke to me as He has
spoken to our older brothers


00:28:25.136 --> 00:28:27.764
since we children started
making sacrifice.


00:28:27.806 --> 00:28:31.708
Praise God.
Praise the Lord.


00:28:31.743 --> 00:28:34.507
And God told me all
that has happened since.


00:28:34.546 --> 00:28:36.207
God said to me,


00:28:36.247 --> 00:28:40.206
"Joseph will take his things
and flee this happy place


00:28:40.251 --> 00:28:43.243
because the fear of me
is no more upon him.


00:28:43.288 --> 00:28:46.917
So take of his life
in punishment, not sacrifice.


00:28:46.958 --> 00:28:49.392
Let not his flesh pollute the corn,


00:28:49.427 --> 00:28:51.793
but cast his body upon the road.


00:28:51.830 --> 00:28:54.230
So thus evermore will Joseph,


00:28:54.265 --> 00:28:56.290
the betrayer of the corn,


00:28:56.334 --> 00:28:59.565
be known as Ahaz, cursed of God."


00:28:59.604 --> 00:29:03.335
Yea, so it is, Joseph, the unbeliever.


00:29:03.374 --> 00:29:05.968
Yea, Ahaz be cursed.


00:29:06.010 --> 00:29:08.001
And the Lord did say,


00:29:08.046 --> 00:29:11.607
"l will send outlanders among you--
a man and a woman--


00:29:11.649 --> 00:29:16.348
and these unbelievers will be
profaners and defilers of the corn.


00:29:16.387 --> 00:29:19.618
Then shall your faith be tested
as it was in the days of the blue man."


00:29:19.657 --> 00:29:22.125
All: The blue man.


00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:24.355
Yea, the blue man.


00:29:25.530 --> 00:29:29.432
He Who Walks Behind The Rows
has protected us from the outside world


00:29:29.467 --> 00:29:33.301
and provided for us since
the oldest amongst us were little.


00:29:33.338 --> 00:29:36.364
But a time of tribulation has come.


00:29:36.407 --> 00:29:38.602
A test is at hand!


00:29:38.643 --> 00:29:40.008
We welcome the test.


00:29:40.044 --> 00:29:42.945
You should not show pride,
Malachai.


00:29:42.981 --> 00:29:46.075
For does not the Bible say that the Lord
will not lift up his countenance


00:29:46.117 --> 00:29:48.745
upon the prideful man?


00:29:49.921 --> 00:29:52.185
What did God say we must do?


00:29:52.223 --> 00:29:56.785
God told me, "Be not like
Ahaz's fate to desert him,


00:29:56.828 --> 00:29:59.695
for My name is strong here,
My power is great.


00:29:59.731 --> 00:30:01.790
I'm the Lord of lords,


00:30:01.833 --> 00:30:04.165
so now you must make
sacrifices to me


00:30:04.202 --> 00:30:08.002
and behold the unbelievers
who've come to fulfill this purpose."


00:30:09.174 --> 00:30:11.665
Make sacrifice.


00:30:11.709 --> 00:30:13.870
Yea!


00:30:15.280 --> 00:30:18.306
Thus shall it be with the outlanders.


00:30:18.349 --> 00:30:21.284
This is the word
of He Who Walks Behind The Rows.


00:30:21.319 --> 00:30:24.049
We do His work
from shine to shadow.


00:30:24.088 --> 00:30:25.715
It is well we do this.


00:30:25.757 --> 00:30:28.749
- Yea, verily.
- Amen.


00:30:28.793 --> 00:30:31.227
( girl laughs )


00:30:37.302 --> 00:30:39.896
- Vicky: Do you smell that?
- Yeah.


00:30:39.938 --> 00:30:41.701
What stinks?


00:30:41.739 --> 00:30:44.708
You were obviously never
a farmer's daughter.


00:30:44.742 --> 00:30:49.270
It's fertilizer. It's the stuff
that makes corn grow green.


00:31:28.586 --> 00:31:31.612
- ( fly buzzing )
- Vicky: Just stop right here.


00:31:31.656 --> 00:31:33.521
Stop.


00:31:43.067 --> 00:31:44.659
( whimpers )


00:31:44.702 --> 00:31:48.297
Let's turn around, Burt. Let's just take
the body back to Grand lsland.


00:31:48.339 --> 00:31:50.864
No. Grand lsland is 70 miles away
in the wrong direction.


00:31:50.909 --> 00:31:52.900
It would look funny
if we brought him there.


00:31:52.944 --> 00:31:54.935
I don't care.


00:31:54.979 --> 00:31:57.209
- What's wrong?
- What do you mean, "What's wrong?"


00:31:57.248 --> 00:31:59.648
This town is empty.
There's nobody here but us.


00:31:59.684 --> 00:32:02.152
Yeah, it sure seems that way.


00:32:02.186 --> 00:32:04.814
It's a one-stoplight town, I agree
with you, but everybody's probably down


00:32:04.856 --> 00:32:07.689
at the town square
having a bake sale or something.


00:32:07.725 --> 00:32:10.353
There's no one here.


00:32:10.395 --> 00:32:12.829
- Do you remember that gas station?
- Yeah, what about it?


00:32:12.864 --> 00:32:17.767
When was the last time you paid
35.9¢ for gas in this country?


00:32:17.802 --> 00:32:20.202
The '60s, maybe.


00:32:20.238 --> 00:32:23.207
We're in the middle of town
and I haven't seen one car moving--


00:32:23.241 --> 00:32:25.334
not one car!


00:32:28.913 --> 00:32:30.847
Where are you--
where are you going?


00:32:30.882 --> 00:32:32.406
I'm gonna go pull
that hair out of your ass.


00:32:32.450 --> 00:32:35.817
I'm gonna go see where everybody is.
The sign says "Open." I'm going in.


00:32:35.853 --> 00:32:39.220
And you're just gonna leave me
alone in the car again, huh?


00:32:39.257 --> 00:32:42.715
You said you wanted
an early lunch stop. Congratulations.


00:32:42.760 --> 00:32:46.719
You've got it. And no talking about
what happened to the boy, all right?


00:32:46.764 --> 00:32:49.961
Huh. If you think so.


00:32:50.001 --> 00:32:52.731
I do. So...


00:32:52.770 --> 00:32:54.761
join me?


00:33:10.021 --> 00:33:11.989
You've got
a busted headlight, mister.


00:33:12.023 --> 00:33:15.254
Blood on it, too. Maybe you hit
a dog or something.


00:33:15.293 --> 00:33:17.261
( whimpers )


00:33:17.295 --> 00:33:19.593
Hmm?


00:33:20.598 --> 00:33:22.691
( whispers )
Look,


00:33:22.734 --> 00:33:24.565
- do you hear it?
- Hear what?


00:33:24.602 --> 00:33:28.163
The nothing. There are no cars.
There are no people.


00:33:28.206 --> 00:33:30.800
There are no fertilizer spreaders.
There's nothing here.


00:33:30.842 --> 00:33:33.834
( distant children playing )


00:33:36.180 --> 00:33:39.741
I hear kids, don't you?


00:33:40.785 --> 00:33:43.049
( creaks )


00:33:43.087 --> 00:33:45.078
( whimpers )


00:33:47.458 --> 00:33:49.289
( flies buzzing )


00:34:16.287 --> 00:34:19.051
( buzzing continues )


00:34:20.525 --> 00:34:25.155
Pardon me, sir. Can I try some
of your 25c sweet potato pie?


00:34:36.908 --> 00:34:39.536
I've been at that
bake sale or football game


00:34:39.577 --> 00:34:42.273
for 12 years now.


00:34:46.384 --> 00:34:50.081
I can't make sense of this.
I'm sure there's people here.


00:34:50.121 --> 00:34:52.089
You know what?
That's what's wrong with you.


00:34:52.123 --> 00:34:55.854
You're always sure.
You spent your whole life being sure.


00:34:55.893 --> 00:34:58.623
Why do you have to be so stubborn?
Why can't you just admit


00:34:58.663 --> 00:35:01.689
that there's something wrong here?
The whole place stinks of it.


00:35:06.571 --> 00:35:08.562
( Vicky panting )


00:35:10.141 --> 00:35:11.768
( softly )
I'm sorry.


00:35:11.809 --> 00:35:14.710
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. Um--


00:35:14.745 --> 00:35:17.612
Why don't we just go find
some local authorities


00:35:17.648 --> 00:35:20.344
and report this accident?


00:35:22.019 --> 00:35:23.680
Okay?


00:35:23.721 --> 00:35:25.382
No.


00:35:25.423 --> 00:35:28.119
- What?
- No.


00:35:28.159 --> 00:35:30.650
There, I said it. No!


00:35:30.695 --> 00:35:33.858
And in a nutshell, why our entire
marriage is falling apart, Burt.


00:35:33.898 --> 00:35:35.832
I said, "No!" No, sir!


00:35:35.867 --> 00:35:38.097
- Just give it a rest.
- I'll give it a rest


00:35:38.136 --> 00:35:39.797
when we're going
the other way, okay?


00:35:39.837 --> 00:35:42.203
Now turn this car around.
Turn it around right now.


00:35:42.240 --> 00:35:45.141
- Let's go and see that lawyer.
- We have a dead child


00:35:45.176 --> 00:35:48.304
in the trunk of our car.
If you wanna go back to l-80


00:35:48.346 --> 00:35:51.372
and walk, that's fine.
I'll pick you up later.


00:35:51.415 --> 00:35:54.248
But do not tell me to drive
70 miles backwards


00:35:54.285 --> 00:35:57.049
and act like we have nothing
but a bag of garbage in our trunk.


00:35:57.088 --> 00:35:59.818
This kid was
some mother's son, Vicky!


00:35:59.857 --> 00:36:02.553
So, I'm gonna find whatever
local justice they have around here


00:36:02.593 --> 00:36:05.790
and report it before whoever killed him
is over the hills and far away!


00:36:05.830 --> 00:36:08.663
- Is that fine by you?
- Yes, sir. Yes, captain, sir.


00:36:08.699 --> 00:36:11.361
I forgot we were back
at Lon Dong or Dung Ho,


00:36:11.402 --> 00:36:13.996
wherever it was
that you won the war.


00:36:14.038 --> 00:36:15.699
It must have been
the Cong, sir.


00:36:15.740 --> 00:36:17.731
Why don't we go back in there,
burn a few hooches


00:36:17.775 --> 00:36:21.802
- and rape a few grandmothers, huh?
- Why don't you stop talking for awhile?


00:36:22.914 --> 00:36:25.576
And put that down.


00:36:25.616 --> 00:36:27.550
- Put it down!
- Tsk.


00:36:27.585 --> 00:36:31.043
You play your games,
and I'll play mine, huh?


00:36:31.088 --> 00:36:35.491
Oh, of course.
That's always the way you play it.


00:36:35.526 --> 00:36:39.155
Let's remember we've got
a prom queen to take care of here.


00:36:42.200 --> 00:36:44.191
( woofs )


00:36:57.882 --> 00:37:00.214
David.


00:37:00.251 --> 00:37:02.981
Get Mark and meet me
at the church.


00:37:03.020 --> 00:37:06.319
Do not let
the outlanders escape.


00:37:08.326 --> 00:37:11.454
I'll get us some
bailing wire then.


00:37:16.033 --> 00:37:18.160
Ben: People gotta come
to Gatlin all the time.


00:37:18.202 --> 00:37:20.966
There must be people who have
friends and relatives here


00:37:21.005 --> 00:37:23.872
and delivery trucks
that come from the outside.


00:37:24.976 --> 00:37:28.002
Not to mention the people just
passing through, like you and me.


00:37:28.045 --> 00:37:30.639
I mean, some of them have to
have noticed something.


00:37:30.681 --> 00:37:33.809
Certain things can't happen--
not in the '70s.


00:37:33.851 --> 00:37:36.786
Whole towns don't just shut down.
What about the state patrol?


00:37:36.821 --> 00:37:38.914
They must cruise through
from time to time.


00:37:38.956 --> 00:37:40.787
The power company, huh?


00:37:40.825 --> 00:37:43.225
Don't you think the power company
would've noticed


00:37:43.261 --> 00:37:46.321
the electricity had been shut off
for 12 long years?


00:37:46.364 --> 00:37:49.197
The stoplight is dead.


00:38:16.193 --> 00:38:18.184
You see that sermon board?


00:38:19.630 --> 00:38:22.622
That's last Sunday.


00:38:22.667 --> 00:38:24.532
Something's happened in this town...


00:38:25.536 --> 00:38:27.800
something wrong.


00:38:27.838 --> 00:38:30.204
In a crisis,
they all collect at the church.


00:38:31.442 --> 00:38:34.502
- "He Who Walks Behind The Rows"?
- Yeah.


00:38:34.545 --> 00:38:38.743
Just one of 9,000 different names
for God in Nebraska, I guess.


00:38:39.750 --> 00:38:42.719
I'm gonna go take a look.
Join me?


00:38:43.921 --> 00:38:46.389
I'm not going in there with you.


00:38:46.424 --> 00:38:49.018
Fine. Do whatever you want.


00:38:51.562 --> 00:38:53.496
I haven't been in a church
since I was a kid.


00:38:53.531 --> 00:38:56.091
I don't wanna be in this church,
I don't wanna be in this town


00:38:56.133 --> 00:38:58.397
and can we just go?!


00:38:58.436 --> 00:39:01.098
I'm just gonna go in
for 10 minutes tops.


00:39:01.138 --> 00:39:03.572
I'll be right back out.


00:39:07.311 --> 00:39:11.338
Okay. That's the deal--
10 minutes.


00:39:11.382 --> 00:39:14.374
I've got my keys.


00:39:14.418 --> 00:39:17.046
If you're not back out here,
I'm gonna drive away.


00:39:18.055 --> 00:39:21.024
All right.
No more games.


00:39:21.058 --> 00:39:25.085
I'm gonna tell you that once--
no more games.


00:39:25.129 --> 00:39:28.428
No games.
10 minutes,


00:39:28.466 --> 00:39:31.435
and then little old Vicky Jean is
gonna put on her boogie shoes.


00:39:31.469 --> 00:39:33.937
I don't think so.


00:39:35.406 --> 00:39:38.637
What are you gonna do? Hmm?


00:39:38.676 --> 00:39:40.769
- Are you gonna assault me? Hmm?
- No.


00:39:40.811 --> 00:39:43.678
Is that what you're gonna do?
Just mug me, take my keys?


00:39:43.714 --> 00:39:46.410
- No, but you think that I would.
- Yeah.


00:39:46.450 --> 00:39:48.281
I think you're
just about capable of that.


00:39:48.319 --> 00:39:50.287
- Yeah?
- Yeah.


00:39:51.622 --> 00:39:54.614
- Give me the bag. Give me the bag!
- Give it to me, you son of a bitch!


00:39:54.658 --> 00:39:56.353
Give me my purse!
Give it to--


00:39:56.394 --> 00:39:58.726
- my-- give me my purse!
- Give me-- give me the bag!


00:39:58.763 --> 00:40:00.355
( sobs )


00:40:06.103 --> 00:40:08.162
Oh, look who has
all the coins in Nebraska.


00:40:08.205 --> 00:40:11.140
You did not have to do that.


00:40:11.175 --> 00:40:14.542
Is that what your sarge
taught you out in the jungle...


00:40:14.578 --> 00:40:17.979
along with how to cut gook tits off
and make moccasins out of them


00:40:18.015 --> 00:40:20.950
in 20 seconds?


00:40:22.520 --> 00:40:24.784
- Just give them back to me.
- No.


00:40:24.822 --> 00:40:26.653
No.


00:40:26.690 --> 00:40:30.751
You'd wait two minutes and decide that
that's long enough. No.


00:40:30.795 --> 00:40:32.854
- No, I wouldn't.
- Yeah! Yeah, you would.


00:40:32.897 --> 00:40:34.728
Then, you'd drive off
laughing, saying,


00:40:34.765 --> 00:40:37.859
"That'll teach that SOB Burt
to mess with the ex-prom queen


00:40:37.902 --> 00:40:41.030
when she wants something."
That's been your whole thesis as a wife,


00:40:41.071 --> 00:40:44.802
hasn't it, Vicky?
"That'll teach Burt to mess with me."


00:40:52.716 --> 00:40:56.311
It's a second honeymoon, huh?


00:40:56.353 --> 00:40:58.753
That's a laugh.


00:41:00.157 --> 00:41:02.182
That I still feel something for you--


00:41:02.226 --> 00:41:07.061
if it means anything-- I think.


00:41:12.736 --> 00:41:14.636
It's okay. You can say it--


00:41:14.672 --> 00:41:16.697
that you hate my guts.


00:41:16.740 --> 00:41:20.267
You hate my guts, and you've--
you've hated them for years.


00:41:20.311 --> 00:41:23.712
No. There's no hate.


00:41:23.747 --> 00:41:26.875
I don't hate. I--


00:41:26.917 --> 00:41:29.909
I feel responsibility.


00:41:31.489 --> 00:41:34.219
I don't even know
what you're talking about.


00:41:34.258 --> 00:41:38.558
No. I don't think that you do.


00:41:40.998 --> 00:41:43.023
I'm gonna go in now.


00:41:43.067 --> 00:41:46.696
Lock all the doors
and roll up the windows.


00:41:46.737 --> 00:41:51.674
Look, let's just get out of town
and find a phone booth, okay?


00:41:51.709 --> 00:41:55.008
- I've got change.
- I'm sick and tired of your tantrums.


00:41:55.045 --> 00:41:58.139
This is not a tantrum.
There is something wrong here.


00:41:58.182 --> 00:42:00.275
( softly )
I can feel it.


00:42:04.021 --> 00:42:05.921
Please.


00:42:05.956 --> 00:42:09.187
Please. Please.


00:42:09.226 --> 00:42:12.662
- No, not this time.
- Please.


00:42:12.696 --> 00:42:15.358
I'm not letting you push
my buttons anymore.


00:42:15.399 --> 00:42:17.390
Please.


00:42:17.434 --> 00:42:19.664
( sobs )
Burt, don't leave me in here.


00:42:19.703 --> 00:42:21.762
Burt!


00:42:21.805 --> 00:42:24.706
Burt, come back here!
Burt, please!


00:42:26.310 --> 00:42:28.471
Son of a bitch!


00:42:28.512 --> 00:42:30.207
Burt, please!
We've gotta get out of here!


00:42:30.247 --> 00:42:32.112
We've gotta
get out of here!


00:42:32.149 --> 00:42:34.117
Burt!


00:42:34.151 --> 00:42:35.914
Come on, we've gotta get outta here.
We've gotta get outta here.


00:42:35.953 --> 00:42:37.944
Please!


00:42:55.306 --> 00:42:58.139
( creaks )


00:43:01.211 --> 00:43:03.338
( loudly )
Hello?


00:43:04.582 --> 00:43:06.573
Anyone here?


00:43:30.374 --> 00:43:32.433
Why are the adults sinners,
Malachai?


00:43:32.476 --> 00:43:33.943
'Cause God said so.


00:43:33.978 --> 00:43:36.139
Does God speak to you
and tell you this, Malachai?


00:43:36.180 --> 00:43:39.581
No. He only speaks to lsaac.


00:43:39.617 --> 00:43:41.710
But on this matter
he has spoken.


00:43:41.752 --> 00:43:43.481
We must sacrifice
the adult sinners


00:43:43.520 --> 00:43:47.786
to protect ourselves from
the outside world. This is our test.


00:43:47.825 --> 00:43:50.919
All: The will of God
be done. Amen.


00:44:44.581 --> 00:44:47.573
( change clinking )


00:44:58.996 --> 00:45:01.260
( sighs )


00:45:31.428 --> 00:45:34.522
Tsk. Damn you, Burt.


00:45:48.912 --> 00:45:50.903
Who's there?


00:45:52.182 --> 00:45:54.173
I know there's--


00:45:54.218 --> 00:45:56.948
I know there's somebody there.
I can hear you.


00:45:56.987 --> 00:45:59.717
( faint whispering )


00:45:59.757 --> 00:46:01.622
Stop playing games.


00:46:03.026 --> 00:46:05.722
Stop playing games!


00:46:05.763 --> 00:46:07.754
( whispering grows louder )


00:46:27.551 --> 00:46:29.712
( whimpers )
Who are you?


00:46:29.753 --> 00:46:31.550
We are your destiny.


00:46:46.503 --> 00:46:49.233
Malachai,
what about the man?


00:46:49.273 --> 00:46:52.299
God has provided
the woman first.


00:47:00.384 --> 00:47:01.908
Burt. Burt!


00:47:17.234 --> 00:47:19.464
( honking )


00:47:24.141 --> 00:47:26.701
( honking continues )


00:47:30.113 --> 00:47:32.343
Burt!


00:47:33.450 --> 00:47:36.715
- Burt!
- ( honking continues )


00:47:36.753 --> 00:47:40.382
"Then the Lord answered Job
out of the whirlwind, and said,


00:47:40.424 --> 00:47:44.417
'Who is this that darkeneth counsel
by words without knowledge?"'


00:47:46.763 --> 00:47:48.924
And please pass the corn.


00:48:12.456 --> 00:48:14.447
( pants )


00:48:23.867 --> 00:48:25.858
( pants )


00:48:29.840 --> 00:48:31.808
What do you want?


00:48:31.842 --> 00:48:34.174
Do you want the body
so you can cover it up?


00:48:34.211 --> 00:48:35.906
It's in the trunk, okay?
Just take it. Take it!


00:48:35.946 --> 00:48:39.006
We don't want his body, sister.


00:48:39.049 --> 00:48:40.914
( sobs )


00:48:40.951 --> 00:48:43.419
I'm not your sister!


00:48:43.453 --> 00:48:45.785
We've come to give you peace.


00:48:45.822 --> 00:48:48.154
No. No.


00:48:48.191 --> 00:48:51.217
Burt! Burt!


00:48:51.261 --> 00:48:54.059
- ( shrieks ) Burt!
- ( children clamor )


00:49:14.151 --> 00:49:15.880
( Vicky screaming ) Burt!


00:49:15.919 --> 00:49:18.717
- ( honking )
- Help me!


00:49:18.755 --> 00:49:21.349
- Help me!
- ( clamoring )


00:49:22.559 --> 00:49:24.857
Help me. Help me.
Help me. Help me.


00:49:24.895 --> 00:49:27.693
Burt. Ah-hh.


00:49:27.731 --> 00:49:29.562
( sobs )


00:49:33.537 --> 00:49:35.562
( gasps )


00:49:35.605 --> 00:49:37.835
( clamoring continues )


00:49:37.874 --> 00:49:40.342
- Burt!
- ( screeching )


00:50:17.214 --> 00:50:19.739
( gasps )


00:50:23.186 --> 00:50:24.551
Burt!


00:50:40.203 --> 00:50:43.229
Ah! Look at me!


00:50:45.909 --> 00:50:48.309
- ( sobs )
- Would you like to pray?


00:50:48.345 --> 00:50:49.369
Pray?


00:50:49.413 --> 00:50:53.281
The time for forgiveness has come
to an end for you, woman.


00:50:53.316 --> 00:50:56.251
The time of judgment
is now at hand.


00:50:56.286 --> 00:50:59.619
- ( panting )
- Hell yawns beneath you!


00:51:01.525 --> 00:51:05.256
- Say your own prayers, brother!
- ( grunts )


00:51:06.963 --> 00:51:09.090
( gunshot )


00:51:09.132 --> 00:51:11.225
- ( children screaming )
- ( Vicky screams )


00:51:17.174 --> 00:51:19.267
( groans )


00:51:23.847 --> 00:51:26.816
Help me, Burt.
Help me, help me.


00:51:26.850 --> 00:51:30.217
( sobbing )


00:51:40.163 --> 00:51:43.530
- ( screams )
- ( knife zings )


00:51:47.270 --> 00:51:49.670
Hey! Stop!


00:51:51.641 --> 00:51:54.838
Vicky!
( pants )


00:51:54.878 --> 00:51:57.176
Don't. My wife's in there.


00:51:59.649 --> 00:52:01.241
No more, brother.


00:52:06.690 --> 00:52:08.555
No!


00:52:12.062 --> 00:52:14.997
( children scream )


00:52:27.944 --> 00:52:31.471
Where is she?
Where have you taken her?


00:52:33.884 --> 00:52:36.375
So you've killed her?


00:52:36.419 --> 00:52:39.547
The time of sacrifice is at hand.


00:52:39.589 --> 00:52:42.854
Sacrifice? Sacrifice?


00:53:26.736 --> 00:53:29.170
( children chanting )
Kill kill kill


00:53:29.206 --> 00:53:32.107
- kill kill kill kill.
- Kill him!


00:53:32.142 --> 00:53:35.475
Kill kill kill kill kill!


00:53:35.512 --> 00:53:37.707
Kill kill.


00:53:37.747 --> 00:53:39.578
- No!
- ( grunts )


00:53:42.552 --> 00:53:45.953
My name is lsaac, chosen by
He Who Walks Behinds The Rows,


00:53:45.989 --> 00:53:49.083
seer and prophet,
guardian of the corn!


00:53:50.760 --> 00:53:52.819
Let my aim be true
if it is thy will!


00:53:54.631 --> 00:53:56.690
( grunts )


00:53:58.368 --> 00:54:02.065
You little bastard.
You little bastard!


00:54:02.105 --> 00:54:04.972
You are a sinner.
You are a defiler of the corn.


00:54:05.008 --> 00:54:07.374
It will do you no good
to curse me.


00:54:07.410 --> 00:54:10.072
Bow to God's will.


00:54:10.113 --> 00:54:11.808
What have you done with my wife?


00:54:11.848 --> 00:54:13.873
Is she dead?


00:54:13.917 --> 00:54:16.886
So it was that
the will of God be done.


00:54:16.920 --> 00:54:18.547
Oh, so you enjoyed it.


00:54:18.588 --> 00:54:21.853
The Lord loveth
a cheerful heart and a glad countenance.


00:54:26.196 --> 00:54:29.996
Watch, all of you!


00:54:32.068 --> 00:54:34.468
( groans softly )


00:54:39.509 --> 00:54:41.704
( gasps )


00:54:41.745 --> 00:54:43.713
( knife clatters )


00:54:43.747 --> 00:54:47.114
You better have more than kitchen knives
and screwdrivers, kiddies.


00:54:47.150 --> 00:54:50.881
You'd better find a flamethrower.
This is my game.


00:54:50.920 --> 00:54:54.151
I've played it before
on better courts than yours.


00:54:54.190 --> 00:54:56.784
The Lord is not mocked.


00:54:56.826 --> 00:54:59.761
Neither am l, sonny.


00:54:59.796 --> 00:55:01.320
Neither am l.
( chuckles )


00:55:01.364 --> 00:55:04.527
I'm leaving now.
I'm gonna go find some people


00:55:04.567 --> 00:55:06.933
and tell them about
what's happening here in Gatlin.


00:55:06.970 --> 00:55:08.631
I don't think
they'll believe me at first--


00:55:08.672 --> 00:55:10.469
I don't think I believe it myself--


00:55:10.507 --> 00:55:12.873
but they will, eventually.


00:55:14.411 --> 00:55:17.903
You guys all belong in an asylum
somewhere-- a loony bin.


00:55:17.947 --> 00:55:21.542
Where are your parents?


00:55:21.584 --> 00:55:26.078
I asked you a question!
Where are your parents?!


00:55:26.122 --> 00:55:28.590
In the corn.


00:55:29.693 --> 00:55:31.923
What does that even mean?


00:55:31.961 --> 00:55:35.920
What have you done?
What's happened here?


00:55:35.965 --> 00:55:37.728
Remand your soul to God,


00:55:37.767 --> 00:55:40.895
for you will stand before
His throne momentarily.


00:55:40.937 --> 00:55:43.997
- ( murmuring )
- I can take you, boy.


00:55:44.040 --> 00:55:46.600
Don't make me prove it.


00:55:54.284 --> 00:55:56.718
God is my strength.


00:55:57.721 --> 00:56:00.121
That's what they told us
in the Marines.


00:56:04.260 --> 00:56:06.490
Kill him! Kill him!


00:56:06.529 --> 00:56:08.656
( grunts )


00:56:13.136 --> 00:56:15.127
( choking )


00:56:24.881 --> 00:56:27.714
How do you like it?


00:56:27.751 --> 00:56:30.015
It's unwise to mess with a guy
who spent three years


00:56:30.053 --> 00:56:32.351
- on jungle patrol.
- ( murmuring )


00:56:32.389 --> 00:56:36.655
Why don't you put that
in your god and smoke it?


00:56:38.128 --> 00:56:41.495
I'm gonna blow the whistle
so hard when I get back.


00:56:43.967 --> 00:56:47.494
- Malachai: Kill the outlander!
- ( children yelling )


00:56:47.537 --> 00:56:48.970
Kill him!


00:57:00.750 --> 00:57:04.015
- Kill the outlander!
- Kill him!


00:57:04.053 --> 00:57:06.851
Kill kill kill kill kill!


00:57:16.399 --> 00:57:18.833
( children shouting )


00:57:21.237 --> 00:57:23.228
( shouting continues )


00:57:44.994 --> 00:57:46.723
All: Ah!


00:57:48.298 --> 00:57:50.198
Whoa.


00:57:52.569 --> 00:57:55.561
( panting )


00:58:03.780 --> 00:58:05.805
- What do we do now?
- I'm not going in there.


00:58:05.849 --> 00:58:07.544
- Not without Malachai and lsaac.
- Me neither.


00:58:07.584 --> 00:58:10.519
- I can't...
- ( murmuring )


00:58:24.534 --> 00:58:28.163
- The Lord is displeased with us.
- Why?


00:58:28.204 --> 00:58:32.334
First Ahaz,
his blood was spilled in the corn.


00:58:32.375 --> 00:58:34.366
Then the man and the woman came.


00:58:34.410 --> 00:58:36.105
They both killed.


00:58:36.145 --> 00:58:38.807
- The man still runs free.
- They will catch him.


00:58:38.848 --> 00:58:41.612
It doesn't matter if they do or not.
The Lord guided my aim--


00:58:41.651 --> 00:58:44.279
and not into his heart,
only into his arm.


00:58:44.320 --> 00:58:47.721
And he took the knife and broke it--
broken in two.


00:58:47.757 --> 00:58:50.191
It was a sign.


00:58:50.226 --> 00:58:51.750
A sign from a sinner?


00:58:51.794 --> 00:58:54.627
The clay knows not
the potter's work.


00:58:54.664 --> 00:58:56.791
All things do the work of God--


00:58:56.833 --> 00:59:00.098
even the sinners,
though they not know it.


00:59:00.136 --> 00:59:03.367
The outlander broke our knives.
We broke our covenant with God


00:59:03.406 --> 00:59:05.966
when you spilled
Ahaz's blood in the corn.


00:59:06.009 --> 00:59:09.445
But he-- Joseph was--
Ahaz was running away.


00:59:09.479 --> 00:59:11.106
Your faith weakened.


00:59:11.147 --> 00:59:14.981
You've led the biggest boys
for three years now.


00:59:15.018 --> 00:59:17.452
Perhaps you've gotten prideful...


00:59:19.122 --> 00:59:22.023
and this is your punishment.


00:59:22.058 --> 00:59:24.925
He Who Walks Behind The Rows
is a jealous God.


00:59:24.961 --> 00:59:27.293
He was old
when Jesus was unborn.


00:59:27.330 --> 00:59:30.595
He is a god of favor,
but He's a god of sacrifice as well.


00:59:30.633 --> 00:59:34.069
- But, lsaac--
- But He's a god of sacrifice as well!


00:59:34.103 --> 00:59:37.504
For what other reason has He allowed
us to survive unseen and unnoticed


00:59:37.540 --> 00:59:41.237
all these years while the world outside
grows more wicked?


00:59:41.277 --> 00:59:43.541
You are old enough to remember
the time of the drought


00:59:43.580 --> 00:59:45.741
before He Who Walks
Behind The Rows.


00:59:45.782 --> 00:59:48.842
But now there's rain and corn,
and everything is good.


00:59:49.886 --> 00:59:53.947
When God speaks to me, Malachai,
will you accept his will?


00:59:53.990 --> 00:59:56.652
Yes, lsaac.


00:59:58.127 --> 01:00:01.893
Praise God!
Praise the Lord!


01:00:03.833 --> 01:00:06.597
Then let us pray.


01:00:09.973 --> 01:00:12.669
The outlander is in God's hands.


01:00:12.709 --> 01:00:15.576
You must give chase
until his time.


01:00:15.612 --> 01:00:17.546
Like the blue man?


01:00:17.580 --> 01:00:20.208
Yes, like the blue man.


01:00:35.698 --> 01:00:38.690
( children murmuring )


01:00:52.115 --> 01:00:54.811
There's an outlander in the corn--


01:00:54.851 --> 01:00:57.183
an unbeliever, like the blue man.


01:00:57.220 --> 01:01:00.212
Children:
The blue man, yea.


01:01:00.256 --> 01:01:03.487
The outlander must be chased
to the clearing of the blue man.


01:01:03.526 --> 01:01:05.721
There he'll be taken in sacrifice.


01:01:05.762 --> 01:01:09.163
Only then will the covenant
be restored.


01:01:09.198 --> 01:01:11.758
This is the word of God.


01:01:11.801 --> 01:01:14.395
First, we'll sing our praise
to the Lord.


01:01:14.437 --> 01:01:17.770
- Will you lead us in hymn?
- Yes, lsaac.


01:01:17.807 --> 01:01:20.833
- Hallelujah!
- Children: Hallelujah!


01:01:20.877 --> 01:01:24.438
¶ Sowing in the morning ¶


01:01:24.480 --> 01:01:26.880
¶ Sowing seeds of kindness ¶


01:01:26.916 --> 01:01:30.943
¶ Sowing in the noontide
and the dewy eve ¶


01:01:30.987 --> 01:01:35.549
¶ Waiting for the harvest
and the time of reaping ¶


01:01:35.591 --> 01:01:40.290
¶ We shall come rejoicing,
bringing in the sheaves ¶


01:01:40.329 --> 01:01:44.095
¶ Bringing in the sheaves,
bringing in the sheaves... ¶


01:01:44.133 --> 01:01:46.658
- Sing on, you little bastards.
- ¶¶ We shall come rejoicing ¶¶


01:01:46.703 --> 01:01:48.694
- ¶¶ Bringing in the sheaves. ¶¶
- There he is! Over there!


01:01:48.738 --> 01:01:49.864
- ( gasps )
- Boys: What?


01:01:49.906 --> 01:01:52.636
- Go get him!
- ( shouting )


01:01:58.748 --> 01:02:01.842
( shouting continues )


01:02:04.821 --> 01:02:07.085
( panting )


01:02:22.004 --> 01:02:23.733
( pants )


01:03:00.743 --> 01:03:02.210
( pants )


01:03:32.408 --> 01:03:34.069
Boy: I hear him!


01:03:44.887 --> 01:03:47.515
Boy #2:
Go go go go!


01:04:25.428 --> 01:04:28.420
- Go go!
- Run run run run run!


01:04:43.546 --> 01:04:45.514
Boy:
I want to be the one who...


01:04:45.548 --> 01:04:48.415
( Burt panting )


01:04:49.986 --> 01:04:52.454
( creaks )


01:05:08.104 --> 01:05:10.834
( boys talking indistinctly )


01:05:23.386 --> 01:05:26.355
Boy: Let me do it.
Let me do it. Let me do it!


01:05:26.389 --> 01:05:27.822
Boy ¶2: No.


01:05:31.661 --> 01:05:33.822
( talking continues )


01:05:33.863 --> 01:05:36.730
( steps approaching )


01:05:45.308 --> 01:05:47.674
Naham.


01:05:48.678 --> 01:05:52.341
- Naham!
- I saw His shadow. I saw it.


01:05:52.381 --> 01:05:55.316
The man? Where?


01:05:55.351 --> 01:05:58.320
Not him, He Who Walks
Behind The Rows.


01:05:58.354 --> 01:06:01.619
- That's blasphemy.
- But, Malachai, I did.


01:06:01.657 --> 01:06:03.921
I saw His shadow.


01:06:07.630 --> 01:06:09.962
I was back there,
walking up the row,


01:06:09.999 --> 01:06:12.593
Iooking for the sinner
or more of his footprints.


01:06:12.635 --> 01:06:16.332
Only I didn't see any footprints because
the ground was all hard and powdery.


01:06:16.372 --> 01:06:19.466
- I know.
- And all of a sudden it got darker


01:06:19.508 --> 01:06:21.442
on my one side
and I looked over


01:06:21.477 --> 01:06:24.241
and it was like the sun
was out on that side.


01:06:24.280 --> 01:06:26.578
I could hear something
walking, breathing,


01:06:26.615 --> 01:06:28.344
and the shadow
came up on the corn.


01:06:28.384 --> 01:06:31.012
I couldn't catch my breath.


01:06:31.053 --> 01:06:33.021
I thought He was coming for me


01:06:33.055 --> 01:06:36.752
because Joseph--
I mean, Ahaz-- was my friend.


01:06:36.792 --> 01:06:40.990
It was He Who Walks
Behind the Rows.


01:06:41.030 --> 01:06:43.692
He passed right by me.


01:06:45.668 --> 01:06:47.966
You had a vision, Naham.


01:06:48.971 --> 01:06:52.099
You're very lucky, if it's true.


01:06:52.141 --> 01:06:55.770
I swear it. I swear it is.


01:06:57.913 --> 01:07:00.211
You may be the next prophet


01:07:00.249 --> 01:07:02.274
once lsaac reaches
the age of favor.


01:07:02.318 --> 01:07:05.981
- I don't wanna be a prophet.
- Do not blaspheme, Naham!


01:07:10.860 --> 01:07:13.226
by the sun.


01:07:16.599 --> 01:07:18.032
Yes, it is.


01:07:18.067 --> 01:07:21.468
We won't stay in the corn after dark
if we don't find the man,


01:07:21.504 --> 01:07:24.166
- will we?
- We will find him.


01:07:24.206 --> 01:07:28.438
- But if we don't?
- We never stay in the corn after dark.


01:07:28.477 --> 01:07:31.412
You know it's not wise.


01:07:31.447 --> 01:07:34.644
Because of... Him?


01:07:34.683 --> 01:07:39.279
- Yes, because of Him.
- He's very old, isn't He?


01:07:39.321 --> 01:07:42.051
Yes, very old,


01:07:42.091 --> 01:07:44.184
and the night is His time.


01:07:57.406 --> 01:08:00.500
- You go that way. I'll go that way.
- Wait, I hear him.


01:08:04.547 --> 01:08:07.482
( panting )


01:08:27.136 --> 01:08:30.003
( men speaking Vietnamese )


01:08:36.846 --> 01:08:39.906
( shouting in Vietnamese )


01:08:50.926 --> 01:08:52.518
Hey, this is my row.


01:08:52.561 --> 01:08:54.825
No, Peter and I were here first.


01:08:54.864 --> 01:08:56.855
He's right, Amos.


01:09:06.275 --> 01:09:08.766
( speaking Vietnamese )


01:09:15.885 --> 01:09:17.352
( speaks Vietnamese )


01:09:17.386 --> 01:09:20.947
( guns firing )


01:09:31.767 --> 01:09:34.258
( firing continues )


01:09:35.871 --> 01:09:38.032
( gasps )


01:09:38.073 --> 01:09:40.769
I see him! I see him!
It's the sinner!


01:09:40.809 --> 01:09:42.970
- He's here! He's here! He's here!
- Shh.


01:09:43.012 --> 01:09:46.413
- ( muffled shouting )
- ( shouting )


01:09:49.451 --> 01:09:51.612
( grunts )


01:09:51.654 --> 01:09:54.282
- ( neck cracks )
- ( Burt groans )


01:09:55.991 --> 01:09:58.551
( children speaking loudly )


01:10:09.071 --> 01:10:12.063
( rocket roars )


01:10:17.379 --> 01:10:19.040
Okay.


01:10:37.132 --> 01:10:39.498
( firing continues )


01:10:51.213 --> 01:10:53.841
( rockets roars, explodes )


01:10:53.882 --> 01:10:56.851
( panting )


01:10:56.885 --> 01:10:58.876
( blood sloshing )


01:11:17.039 --> 01:11:19.701
Come on!


01:11:19.742 --> 01:11:22.734
- Come on! ( echoes )
- ( bell ringing )


01:12:03.619 --> 01:12:05.610
They're back!


01:12:07.156 --> 01:12:09.624
( murmuring )


01:12:12.895 --> 01:12:15.193
Take these to the others.


01:12:17.866 --> 01:12:20.232
It's Amos.


01:12:24.139 --> 01:12:26.232
( coos )


01:12:28.243 --> 01:12:31.110
( murmuring continues )


01:13:11.653 --> 01:13:13.951
- ( rips )
- ( groans )


01:13:21.029 --> 01:13:24.021
( murmuring )


01:13:32.307 --> 01:13:33.968
( bangs )


01:13:34.009 --> 01:13:36.705
Let us pray.


01:13:40.549 --> 01:13:43.518
( laughing softly )


01:13:43.552 --> 01:13:44.985
( whispers )
Shut up.


01:13:45.020 --> 01:13:47.648
( giggles softly )


01:14:07.676 --> 01:14:10.668
( crickets chirping )


01:14:20.389 --> 01:14:23.790
- ( coos )
- lsaac: "Be fruitful and multiply


01:14:23.826 --> 01:14:28.525
as the corn multiplies, that my favor
be shewn you and be upon you.


01:14:28.564 --> 01:14:31.465
Dear God, we beg
thy blessing on the crop.


01:14:31.500 --> 01:14:33.730
In the name of He Who Walks
Behind The Rows."


01:14:33.769 --> 01:14:35.794
All: Amen.


01:14:35.838 --> 01:14:38.363
The time of fertilization has come.


01:15:04.600 --> 01:15:06.966
( rustling )


01:16:05.460 --> 01:16:08.190
( gasps, pants )


01:16:09.231 --> 01:16:11.358
Oh shit.


01:16:16.905 --> 01:16:18.805
( moaning )


01:16:30.752 --> 01:16:34.153
Dead!
( shouting )


01:16:34.189 --> 01:16:36.123
Ah! God!


01:16:36.158 --> 01:16:38.183
( moaning )


01:16:40.662 --> 01:16:44.359
God! Ah!


01:16:46.635 --> 01:16:47.966
( shouting continues )


01:16:53.041 --> 01:16:55.271
( screaming )


01:16:55.310 --> 01:16:56.834
( shouting )


01:17:33.515 --> 01:17:35.881
( static screeching )


01:17:41.890 --> 01:17:44.859
He's here! It's the sinner!
It's the sinner!


01:17:46.061 --> 01:17:48.825
God is my strength.


01:17:48.864 --> 01:17:51.594
It was He Who Walks
Behind The Rows.


01:17:55.037 --> 01:17:58.097
Children:
The blue man. Yea, the blue man.


01:17:58.140 --> 01:18:01.837
( Vicky screams )


01:18:02.044 --> 01:18:04.410
( panting )


01:18:10.252 --> 01:18:12.914
It's due west
back to the highway, right?


01:18:12.954 --> 01:18:14.615
Right.


01:18:20.328 --> 01:18:22.023
I'll hitch a ride.


01:18:22.064 --> 01:18:24.589
I'll make
some phone calls.


01:18:24.633 --> 01:18:26.601
( rustles )


01:18:26.635 --> 01:18:29.798
Which way is it
back to the road?


01:18:31.239 --> 01:18:34.470
Okay, I can go west by the stars.


01:18:35.711 --> 01:18:37.440
I went on 61 patrols.


01:18:37.479 --> 01:18:40.277
- ( rustles, creaks )
- I came back from every one of them.


01:18:40.315 --> 01:18:42.078
( rustles )


01:18:42.117 --> 01:18:43.744
( sniffs )


01:18:43.785 --> 01:18:45.309
'Cause I've got
a compass in my head.


01:18:45.353 --> 01:18:48.413
I'm gonna get out.
I'm gonna get out of here.


01:18:48.457 --> 01:18:50.391
( rustles )


01:18:50.425 --> 01:18:53.394
- Stop talking to yourself.
- ( rustles )


01:18:53.428 --> 01:18:55.089
Stop talking to yourself.


01:19:27.129 --> 01:19:28.824
( swishes )


01:19:34.002 --> 01:19:36.562
( panting )


01:19:57.225 --> 01:20:00.592
- ( crackles )
- ( grunts )


01:20:24.820 --> 01:20:27.687
( creaking )


01:20:31.026 --> 01:20:33.017
( crackling )


01:20:42.103 --> 01:20:45.072
( crackling continues )


01:20:45.106 --> 01:20:47.097
( groans )


01:20:52.581 --> 01:20:54.776
( groans )


01:20:56.718 --> 01:20:59.949
- ( rustles )
- ( knife clangs )


01:21:30.051 --> 01:21:31.746
( sighs )


01:21:31.786 --> 01:21:34.050
( whispers )
Oh my God.


01:21:34.089 --> 01:21:35.954
Oh my God!


01:21:35.991 --> 01:21:38.516
( wheezes )
Oh my God.


01:21:38.560 --> 01:21:41.791
Vicky. Vicky.


01:21:55.210 --> 01:21:58.008
( crackling )


01:21:59.314 --> 01:22:00.838
Who's there?


01:22:00.882 --> 01:22:03.874
- Who's there?!
- ( crackling continues )


01:22:05.186 --> 01:22:08.053
Come out where I can see you,
you black pajama'd bastards!


01:22:08.089 --> 01:22:11.650
( rustling, crackling )


01:22:12.827 --> 01:22:16.490
Come out here!
Come out here and look at me!


01:22:18.967 --> 01:22:21.959
( louder, faster rustling )


01:22:42.991 --> 01:22:45.459
Hey, Burt.


01:22:45.493 --> 01:22:49.554
Come on, it's not so bad.


01:22:49.597 --> 01:22:52.566
Being sacrificed by devil
pagan children in the corn--


01:22:52.600 --> 01:22:55.194
- it's not so bad.
- ( static screeching )


01:22:57.072 --> 01:22:59.700
Having your eyes ripped
out of your skull,


01:22:59.741 --> 01:23:01.402
- according to the laws of Moses--
- ( grunts )


01:23:01.443 --> 01:23:03.809
it's not so bad.


01:23:03.845 --> 01:23:05.972
- ( man screams )
- It's all right.


01:23:06.014 --> 01:23:07.982
- Join me?
- ( thunders )


01:23:08.016 --> 01:23:10.814
( shouts )


01:23:10.852 --> 01:23:13.184
( knife clangs )


01:23:22.364 --> 01:23:24.059
( buzzes )


01:23:25.100 --> 01:23:29.196
Last night, He Who Walks Behind
The Rows spoke to me in a dream,


01:23:29.237 --> 01:23:31.933
and I did fall down
upon my knees in fright


01:23:31.973 --> 01:23:36.273
and hide my eyes lest the terror
of His face strike me dead.


01:23:36.311 --> 01:23:40.748
He is much displeased
with this sacrifice.


01:23:42.717 --> 01:23:46.380
And the Lord did say, "Have I not
given you this place of killing


01:23:46.421 --> 01:23:48.355
so that you might make
sacrifice here?


01:23:48.390 --> 01:23:51.257
Have I not shewn you favor?


01:23:51.292 --> 01:23:53.055
But I did give you a test.


01:23:53.094 --> 01:23:56.461
Two outlanders did come--
a man and a woman.


01:23:56.498 --> 01:23:58.966
But this man has made
a blasphemy within me


01:23:59.000 --> 01:24:01.491
and did cause confusion
among you.


01:24:01.536 --> 01:24:03.766
This man was strong
in his evil.


01:24:04.773 --> 01:24:07.970
And so then I've completed
this sacrifice myself


01:24:08.009 --> 01:24:10.807
Iike the blue man who tried
to escape many years ago."


01:24:10.845 --> 01:24:13.473
The blue man.
Yea, the blue man.


01:24:13.515 --> 01:24:16.916
"And so now
the age of favor is lowered


01:24:16.951 --> 01:24:19.215
from 19 planting harvests to 18.


01:24:19.254 --> 01:24:23.054
Each and every one of you will walk
into the corn at dusk


01:24:23.091 --> 01:24:25.286
upon your 18th birthday


01:24:25.326 --> 01:24:29.092
and He Who Walks Behind
The Rows will find you,


01:24:29.130 --> 01:24:31.064
and you will walk with Him."


01:24:31.099 --> 01:24:33.829
So the Lord told me.


01:24:41.976 --> 01:24:45.275
I obey the word of God.


01:24:49.417 --> 01:24:52.477
- Praise God!
- All: Praise God.


01:24:52.520 --> 01:24:56.183
May the favor of He Who Walks
Behind The Rows be shewn


01:24:56.224 --> 01:24:59.057
- and be upon you.
- Amen.


01:25:53.748 --> 01:25:56.342
Scarecrow!


01:29:23.057 --> 01:29:26.049
( steps approaching )


01:29:57.892 --> 01:30:00.122
Never mind.


01:30:01.496 --> 01:30:03.157
If it is God's will,


01:30:03.197 --> 01:30:07.258
the children will continue on
as always, Ruth.


01:30:08.403 --> 01:30:11.304
If it's God's will, yes.


01:30:12.473 --> 01:30:14.134
Then why do you fear?


01:30:14.175 --> 01:30:16.837
- I fear nothing.
- Please, Malachai.


01:30:16.878 --> 01:30:18.743
I obey the will of God.


01:30:18.780 --> 01:30:22.443
My birthday will come
in October after the harvest.


01:30:22.483 --> 01:30:25.316
I barely lose one month.


01:30:25.353 --> 01:30:28.516
Amos is losing almost
his entire 18th year.


01:30:28.556 --> 01:30:32.322
If this is the will of God,
I wish there were no God!


01:30:32.360 --> 01:30:34.726
Do not blaspheme!


01:30:45.706 --> 01:30:49.107
Have a fine son, Ruth,


01:30:49.143 --> 01:30:52.203
and raise him to love religion
and to hate the world.


01:30:56.884 --> 01:30:59.318
Promise me.


01:30:59.353 --> 01:31:02.117
I-- I can't.


01:31:22.677 --> 01:31:25.271
Amos:
It's night now.


01:31:27.982 --> 01:31:30.212
His time.


01:31:31.452 --> 01:31:34.080
I know, Amos.


01:31:37.525 --> 01:31:40.221
( sobs )
Goodbye, Malachai.

